  "term": "semantic memory",
  "definition": "Semantic memory is the part of memory for concepts and their meaning-related features. It is thought to depend on stored knowledge representations working together with control processes that help select, retrieve, use, and monitor relevant meaning while suppressing irrelevant information.",
